Alright, folks, let's address the elephant in the room. And I mean... *LOOK* at this elephant. This isn't your average, gray, "remembers where the waterhole is" kind of elephant. This is the "I just got back from a three-day music festival and I am seeing SOUNDS" elephant.

This is what happens when a hot air balloon has a baby with a Lite-Brite. It's wearing more patterns than my grandma's entire collection of fine china. You know it’s a wild party when the largest animal in the room looks like it got into a fight with a blue Sharpie and a string of Christmas lights... and *loved* it.

Look at him! He's not just standing there; he's *glowing* with the confidence of someone who knows their electric bill is being paid by the city.

And what's with the little glowing green things on the floor? Are those alien lollipops? Is that what it eats? I feel like if you lick one, you either start understanding quantum physics or you wake up in another dimension with a tattoo of this exact elephant on your back. No in-between.

You see all the people just standing there, staring. They're not sure if it's art or if they've accidentally wandered into the world's most fabulous bug zapper. Either way, you can't look away. It’s the elephant that never forgets... to be the center of attention.
